 <peijin@ustc.edu>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:51:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 31/35] metal: quiet by default, gate backend notice behind
 TIMING

The per-inversion 'used/refused' line now prints only on refusal or
with MX_METAL_DEBUG_TIMING. All progress/timing output was already
env-gated; error and refusal paths stay unconditional (diagnostic).

diff --git a/wgridder/wgridder.h b/wgridder/wgridder.h
index 820bef11..6ab2f383 100644
--- a/wgridder/wgridder.h
+++ b/wgridder/wgridder.h
@@ -414,9 +414,10 @@ class WGridder final : public WGridderBase {
                        "rel_max=%.4g n=%zu\n",
                        max_ref, max_diff, rms / max_ref, max_diff / max_ref, n);
         }
-        std::fprintf(stderr, "[mx-metal] inversion %s (%zu rows, %zu x %zu)\n",
-                     metal_done ? "used" : "refused, falling back to ducc0", n_rows,
-                     trimmed_width_, trimmed_height_);
+        if (!metal_done || std::getenv("MX_METAL_DEBUG_TIMING") != nullptr)
+          std::fprintf(stderr, "[mx-metal] inversion %s (%zu rows, %zu x %zu)\n",
+                       metal_done ? "used" : "refused, falling back to ducc0", n_rows,
+                       trimmed_width_, trimmed_height_);
         if (metal_done) {
           for (size_t k = 0; k < trimmed_width_ * trimmed_height_; ++k) image_[k] += tdirty.raw(k);
           return;
